			<div class="content" id="post-content-4474540">
									

<p>I have no idea what's going on, but unlike most other times wherein that's true, I'm absolutely loving this! The Magistereum is my new favorite GoI, that's for sure. Even if you don't get the -5000 slot (which, tbh I don't think is likely), then I hope you stick with this and write lots more!</p>
<p>I have only three sticking points -</p>
<p>1) Why would UNESCO call the Foundation, instead of the GOC? And why would the Foundation find out about this through them, rather than through watching the news, or social media?</p>
<p>2) This anomaly is very LOUD and public. Seems like a nightmare to contain, since it's at a tourist hot-spot. But, I couldn't find any consideration for that in the article. What gives?</p>
<p>3) I think this should be a Keter class, since Thorim could destroy the world in a few years, and because it's at a public landmark, and because containment seems pretty complicated (though apparently reliable).</p>
<p>Anyway, upvoted! Thanks for writing!</p>

