<p>I'm a little torn on this. While I enjoy the worldbuilding, as I made clear when greenlighting your pitch, I would have really appreciated if there was more of it done like the last addendum instead of in the form of exposition dumps in the interviews. There's also some issues with tone throughout, but seeing English is your second language, I'll cut you some slack.</p>
<p>I'm not gonna lie, the colored text really irks me. I guess this type of stylistic stuff works when used sparingly and with purpose, as in <em>House of Leaves</em>, but here it ends up being used excessively and seemingly without a method to the madness. Unless there's an actual reason as to why it's there, it comes across to me as nothing more than a gimmick. Also, readers are usually inclined to find patterns in stylistic deviations like this, so when it turns out there's none, it ends up being confusing and disorienting to read.</p>
<p>-1 for now, sorry.</p>

