<p>[Noting I got a PM request to take a look]</p>
<p>This is&#8230;definitely a concept which has some really good ideas included in it, and there's some really neat world-building in here, but it feels&#8230;poorly executed?</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Weaknesses</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><em>Uh, I hope you don't take this as me dunking on your SCP here: I'm trying to illustrate a whole bunch of stuff which doesn't work for me and by extension how it could be improved.</em></p>
<p>The ConProcs feel a little overwritten: they're mostly good ideas but there's a few details that might be best left assumed, e.g, the armed guards and the socialisation for good behaviour aspects<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-865344-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-865344-1')">1</a></sup>? I think the note about the lights being changed so they don't emit UV can also be implied from the mention of them not being exposed to UV?</p>
<p>The Description is worse for this: you have 9 paragraphs of text just explaining what the anomaly is before you even kick off the story and it's too much. It's generally boring to read, and it feels like there's perhaps a few too many anomalous things kicking about that don't have much importance (e.g, the bit where it turns stuff into 5 dimensional things; the secondary anomalous properties of the -3 instance; the plants as well: they feel symbolically important perhaps but they're over-mentioned and I don't quite get the symbolism).</p>
<p>Also, while you can get away with referring to subinstances (e.g, SCP-5536-2) in the ConProcs without defining them, you really should define what they are before mentioning what they do.</p>
<p>After this, there's a really large section about how this was discovered to kick the story off and it's&#8230;technically fine? I feel like 5 pretty big paragraphs about what exactly happened to all the tourists around the SCP is a bit excessive and I'd really suggest trimming it down.</p>
<p>The Observation logs feel unnecessary: they basically just reveal what the description already told us about the dreams, without adding any extra detail other than that the generic &quot;astronomical events&quot; are specifically &quot;lunar and solar eclipses&quot;; but that info is already hinted towards by the big focus on what happens during both of them in the ConProcs/Description?</p>
<p>The Testing logs also feel a little unnecessary: there's some cool stuff mentioned in them but they don't feel&#8230;hugely important? At the end of the day, this is largely a story about extradimensional beings with a portal, and the testing logs mostly reinforce that the portal is dangerous to observe?</p>
<p>I'm gonna take a quick formatting thing here: the yellow you use e.g, in [DATA EXPUNGED], and the blue you use in &quot;river&quot; are both&#8230;really hard to read? Like I get the colours are symbolically important and hint at who is saying what, but it really needs more contrast(?) with the white background for it to work (it might be worth checking out <a href="/taboo">taboo</a> here btw: it uses colour in a similar way and you can see how it's a lot easier to read because it sticks to pretty dark colours; but you also have the option to use different font styling as shown in the colour blind accessible variant of it).</p>
<p>Uh, everything after the end of the testing logs is generally pretty good and it's very much the strongest aspect of the SCP: unfortunately, you've buried it under a lot of cruft that's not very interesting. The main problem with that is that I really don't have a feel for the stakes here? It feels like this is a thing where I should be acutely aware that the world is being balanced on a knife-edge because of, but instead it feels&#8230;abstract and not quite tangible enough?</p>
<p>The writing is super-patchy too: there's a lot of weird phrasings and iffy grammar and I really did attempt a line-by-line but it took me ages and I don't feel like that's the biggest issue here.</p>
<p>Uh, I ended up downvoting this largely because while the core idea is good, the overall display is just&#8230;filled with too much stuff that didn't work for me, and the good doesn't feel good enough to overcome that :(</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
