<p>Thanks for responding! Don't worry, I don't feel like getting dunked on. After all, I have summoned you to give your criticism on my finished product, regardless of how harsh it might seem.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Okay</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Let's&nbsp;see</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The ConProcs feel a little overwritten: they're mostly good ideas but there's a few details that might be best left assumed, e.g, the armed guards and the socialisation for good behaviour aspects1? I think the note about the lights being changed so they don't emit UV can also be implied from the mention of them not being exposed to UV?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I thought so too, but one of the early draft reviewers, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-fullham" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1989312); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1989312&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1581599160" alt="Doctor Fullham" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1989312)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-fullham" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1989312); return false;">Doctor Fullham</a></span>, mentioned that there should be some consideration on how the Foundation keep him from exploding and treat him like a somewhat normal human being. So, I'm feeling a little split here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also, while you can get away with referring to subinstances (e.g, SCP-5536-2) in the ConProcs without defining them, you really should define what they are before mentioning what they do.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah, sorry! Since the -2 instances don't really need any procedures (other than <em>don't</em> go near it), I figured that they probably shouldn't be mentioned in the ConProc. I might be wrong, and I usually am.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The Description is worse for this: you have 9 paragraphs of text just explaining what the anomaly is before you even kick off the story and it's too much.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I wasn't really sure how to describe 3 slightly connected anomalies with wildly different properties, so that was something I burdened myself with. I don't really have a clue on trimming them, for I am a man of wasteful words.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I feel like 5 pretty big paragraphs about what exactly happened to all the tourists around the SCP is a bit excessive and I'd really suggest trimming it down.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Perhaps. I'm not really sure how, though, because I may have put too many things happening in quick succession, so I just inevitably cornered myself once again.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The Observation logs feel unnecessary: they basically just reveal what the description already told us about the dreams, without adding any extra detail other than that the generic &quot;astronomical events&quot; are specifically &quot;lunar and solar eclipses&quot;; but that info is already hinted towards by the big focus on what happens during both of them in the ConProcs/Description?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The observation logs are mostly for going slightly in depth on the &quot;long dreams&quot; property, but of course, me being me, it ends up feeling bloated.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The Testing logs also feel a little unnecessary: there's some cool stuff mentioned in them but they don't feel…hugely important? At the end of the day, this is largely a story about extradimensional beings with a portal, and the testing logs mostly reinforce that the portal is dangerous to observe?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Cool stuff for the sake of having cool stuff. Always comes back to bite me every time.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The main problem with that is that I really don't have a feel for the stakes here? It feels like this is a thing where I should be acutely aware that the world is being balanced on a knife-edge because of, but instead it feels…abstract and not quite tangible enough?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah, using partial dream logic is something I would probably never forgive myself for. Surrealism has never been my strongest card, so for that, pardon me.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The writing is super-patchy too: there's a lot of weird phrasings and iffy grammar and I really did attempt a line-by-line but it took me ages and I don't feel like that's the biggest issue here.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Some stuff are deliberate, like the words <strong>niatruc</strong> and <strong>éta répsax</strong>, others are just stupid pitfalls I keep on stumbling upon.</p>
<hr />
<p>I am fully aware that the final addendum and the message to the Timmūs-Operative are the only decent saving graces here, but I'll see what I can do to improve it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thanks for the crit!</p>

							</div>

